{"name":"Fuchsia Pheromone","hex":"#9f4cb7","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"fuchsia","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A popular garden plant, of the genus Fuchsia, of the Onagraceae family, shrubs with red, pink or purple flowers.","A purplish-red colour, the color of fuchsin, an aniline dye."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a purplish-red colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fuchsia"},{"term":"pheromone","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A chemical secreted by an animal, especially an insect, that affects the development or behavior of other members of the same species, functioning often as a means of attracting a member of the opposite sex."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pheromone"}],"entries":[{"title":"Fuchsia","blocks":[{"text":"Fuchsia is a genus of flowering plants that consists mostly of shrubs or small trees."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Brincos_De_Princesa.jpg/330px-Brincos_De_Princesa.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fuchsia","wikidata":"Q161066"},{"title":"Pheromone","blocks":[{"text":"In biology, a pheromone is a chemical that is secreted or excreted by an organism, which triggers a social response in members of the same species. There are alarm pheromones, food trail pheromones, sex pheromones, and many others that affect behavior or physiology. Pheromones are used by many organisms, from basic unicellular prokaryotes to complex multicellular eukaryotes. Their use among insects has been particularly well documented. In addition, some vertebrates, plants and ciliates communicate by using pheromones. The ecological functions and evolution of pheromones are a major topic of research in the field of chemical ecology."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/70/Nasinov_9024.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pheromone","wikidata":"Q167377"},{"title":"Fuchsia (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Fuchsia is a vivid pinkish–red color, named after the color of the flower of the fuchsia plant, which was named by a French botanist, Charles Plumier, after the 16th-century German botanist Leonhart Fuchs."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/DoubleFuchsias_wb.jpg/330px-DoubleFuchsias_wb.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fuchsia_(color)","wikidata":"Q5005364"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Bloemknop_van_een_Fuchsia_cultivar_Origami._28-06-2026_%28d.j.b.%29.jpg/500px-Bloemknop_van_een_Fuchsia_cultivar_Origami._28-06-2026_%28d.j.b.%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Bloemknop_van_een_Fuchsia_cultivar_Origami._28-06-2026_%28d.j.b.%29.jpg/1280px-Bloemknop_van_een_Fuchsia_cultivar_Origami._28-06-2026_%28d.j.b.%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Bloemknop_van_een_Fuchsia_cultivar_Origami._28-06-2026_%28d.j.b.%29.jpg/500px-Bloemknop_van_een_Fuchsia_cultivar_Origami._28-06-2026_%28d.j.b.%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":" Flower bud of a Fuchsia cultivar Origami.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABloemknop_van_een_Fuchsia_cultivar_Origami._28-06-2026_(d.j.b.).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/Selasphorus_flammula_424635137.jpg/500px-Selasphorus_flammula_424635137.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/Selasphorus_flammula_424635137.jpg/1280px-Selasphorus_flammula_424